<title>USA: Bonneville offers no surplus power for Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Bonneville offers no surplus power for Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered no surplus power for Tuesday preschedulings, the federal agency said Monday.</p>
<p>BPA has not been in the market with spot power since late last week, when it was offering up to 200 megawatts (MW).</p>
<p>Before it withdrew from offering surplus power for Saturday through Monday, BPA offered firm power during heavy-load hours at $25.50 per megawatt hour (MWh) in the Northwest and $26.50 for COB/NOB deliveries. Firm light-load power was offered at $19.50 for Friday.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
